==Restrictions==
Cat Deploy Cost: Only 600¢ or less

==Battleground==
*2 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Zyclone]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*8 [[Zomboe]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*8 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*8 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*8 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 213.33 seconds<sup>6,400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*8 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 266.67 seconds<sup>8,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage greatly limits the number of units you can use compared to [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)|Unholy Tempest]], most notably taking away [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and several Uber Rare Cats, even the cheapest ones. Just like the original stage, [[Samurai Cat (Special Cat)|Pastry Cat]] can also be usable with a Slow Effect Up [[Cat Combo|Combo]], beating the stage quickly and Z-Killing Zyclone is crucial to not fight the onslaught of peons that come out when you take too long.

===='''Recommended Units'''====
*[[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] - Just as useful as in the previous stage, its spammability, high attack rate and Freezing capabilities make it a mainstay when it comes to Crowd-Controlling and finishing off Zyclone with Z-Kill.
*[[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]] - Unlike Weedwacker, his chances to proc are much higher, but is also risky to use due to being able to pin Zyclone at the base and making your units clip into its range.
*[[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] - With a very powerful weaken and Surge to proc even more Weaken towards peons, he is an absolute menace for stalling Zyclone, but beware his uptime isn't 100% without combos and the [[Antimatter Fruit]]. Bring him with other Crowd-Controllers to permanently stunlock the Zyclone. Pre-TF is not recommended due to his insanely slow speed and luring being incredibly risky due to burrowing peons.
*[[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] - More so useful for the Peons and DPS as Zyclone deals too much damage for Shigong to handle, unless you weaken Zyclone with Headmaster Cat Jobs.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - With a low cooldown, high DPS and survive, she is quite useful to bring here given the lack of options. While she lacks Zombie Killer, you are likely going to bring Weedwacker and Shigong to get the Z-Kill in.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] - Cheap enough to be brought here, it's got decent attack power to chip down the Zyclone and incoming peons. Like Cameraman, however, he lacks Z-Kill.
*[[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Sexy Legs]] - Similar to Manic Macho Legs but with higher damage output.

